  "entries": {
    "buy": {
      "word": "BUY",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To acquire the ownership of (property) by giving an accepted price or consideration therefor, or by agreeing to do so; to acquire by the payment of a price or value; to purchase; -- opposed to sell. Buy what thou hast no need of, and ere long thou wilt sell thy necessaries. B. Franklin.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To acquire or procure by something given or done in exchange, literally or figuratively; to get, at a cost or sacrifice; to buy pleasure with pain. Buy the truth and sell it not; also wisdom, and instruction, and understanding. Prov. xxiii. 23. To buy again. See Againbuy. [Obs.] Chaucer. yield by some consideration; as, to buy off conscience. (b) To detach by a consideration given; as, to buy off one from a party. the share or shares of in a stock, fund, or partnership, by which the seller is separated from the company, and the purchaser takes his place; as, A buys out B. (c) To purchase the entire stock in trade and the good will of a business. to make payment at a future day. right of purchasing, at a fixed price, at a future time.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To negotiate or treat about a purchase. I will buy with you, sell with you. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
